So I currently play with a variety of challenges to make Nethack a
little more interesting for my thoroughly spoiled self and have come
to a point where I think modifying the game will be the most
satisfying way to implement my designs on gameplay.

Well, there are many neat patches kickin around, it's easy to not
wish / genocide / or chat to priests, and changing the rewards for
various special levels is fairly straightforward, but I currently play
characters who do not eat corpses that could grant them an intrinsic
(a list gleaned from this very newsgroup helps me with that) nor quaff
any potions of healing save those which are known to be cursed.

I know the intrinsics issue is one of the main difficulties in the
vegan challenge, but I don't want to stick with an official challenge
just to avoid the resistance transfer. As for the !oHealing bit, after
you've ascended your first -70AC, 900hp flying, invisible, very fast,
frost brand / silver saber two-weaponing, orb of fate protected
Valkyrie once, you don't really feel like doing it again, you know?

So is there an easy way to modify these functions in the source? I
don't know C (and according to Rob Ellwood, trying to learn C by
editing Nethack source code is masochistic), but I'm just starting
that journey (viz. programming) with a little bash scripting and man
